      "narrative": "Mara Venn's fingers tap against her cup as she considers your question. She opens her mouth, then stops, squinting at a water stain on the ceiling as if the answer might be written there.\n\n\"The lock...\" She trails off, frowning. \"You know, I think I heard something about that. There was a lockwright, someone who kept the mechanism working. Before it was sealed, I mean. But the name...\" She rubs her temple. \"Gods, it's right there. Toran might know, he keeps the records\u2014or what's left of them.\"\n\nShe gestures vaguely toward the corner where Toran Vex sits hunched over a stack of papers, ink-stained cuffs brushing the table. But her brow stays furrowed, like she's still chasing the thought she couldn't quite catch.\n\n<ref_entity>..."
