      "narrative": "The walk back is quiet. The road curves past the shuttered houses, the woodsmoke still hanging in the air, and the Copper Finch's copper lamps come into view, their flames guttering against the grey morning. The door groans as you push it open.\n\nThe warmth hits you first\u2014the hearth fire crackling, the smell of old ale and beeswax. A few patrons nurse breakfast cups at scattered tables. Mara Venn is still at her table near the window, a fresh cup of tea steaming in front of her, a small leather notebook open beside it. She looks up as you enter, her sharp eyes tracking your approach.\n\n\"Back already,\" she says, not quite a question. \"Didn't find what you were looking for?\"\n\nShe gestures to the empty chair across from her. The notebook lies open\u2014pages filled with her neat, angled handwriting, a sketch of the Ash Gate's lock mechanism tucked into the margin.\n\n<ref_entity entity_id=\"mara-venn\" dialogue_indices=\"[1,2]\" dialogue_emotions=\"[\"curious\", \"welcoming\"]\"></ref_entity>..."
